  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Design and validation phase in24</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Small and medium enterprises (SMEs) in the energy access sector are instrumental in achieving universal access to clean and affordable energy. However, many of these SMEs operate under the PAYGo (Pay-As-You-Go) business model, which presents persistent challenges - particularly in managing end-user credit risk. Since 2017, the PAYGo Lab has worked with dozens of companies and their investors to better understand and address these credit-related issues. While some improvements have been achieved, they have not been sufficient to resolve core vulnerabilities in the PAYGo model. Over-financing remains a significant problem, with over 50% of customers failing to complete payments for their systems. A structural shift is urgently needed. The in24 model responds to this need by facilitating responsible asset financing for underserved customers, while enabling companies to streamline operations and unlock working capital. Ultimately, in24 aims to serve as a bridge between local financial institutions, international funders, and rural customers - unlocking capital through a model that combines risk mitigation with operational efficiency.</narrative>
  </description>
